From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:27:55 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 65/82] Plutonium: keys an input method passes on reach every
 app

With an input method engine, which answers asynchronously, the keys it
doesn't take (Enter, Backspace and arrows outside a composition, every
shortcut) reach Exo's Keyboard after Seat::DidProcessEvent(), with no
physical code. Keyboard then dropped them unless the focused surface was
an ARC or Crostini app's, so a GTK, Qt or foot window got no keys at all
while an extension IME was current. In Plutonium sessions every surface
now counts, and such a key's own code stands in for the physical one.
---
 components/exo/keyboard.cc | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/components/exo/keyboard.cc b/components/exo/keyboard.cc
index 681559132d..4ccfd12b22 100644
--- a/components/exo/keyboard.cc
+++ b/components/exo/keyboard.cc
@@ -107,6 +107,13 @@ bool ProcessAcceleratorIfReserved(Surface* surface, ui::KeyEvent* event) {
 // TODO(yhanada, https://crbug.com/847500): Remove this when we find a way
 // to fix https://crbug.com/847500 without breaking ARC apps/Lacros browser.
 bool IsImeSupportedSurface(Surface* surface) {
+  // EXO-IME: in Plutonium every app is one. With an input method engine
+  // (which answers asynchronously), a key it passes on arrives after
+  // Seat::DidProcessEvent() and has no physical code; it is dropped unless
+  // the surface counts as supporting IME.
+  if (EmbeddedWindows::HideWindows()) {
+    return true;
+  }
   aura::Window* window = surface->window();
   while (window) {
     const auto app_type = window->GetProperty(chromeos::kAppTypeKey);
